  "findings": [
    "1. engine/tests/test_model_catalog.py::test_remove_is_refused_for_a_file_a_running_graph_reads_in_this_process_or_another fails on every run on this PC (twice in a row). After holder.kill() and holder.wait(), Windows has not yet released the killed process's msvcrt lock, so the next models.remove still answers in_use (retry: true); reproduced outside the repo, the remove succeeded 0.27 s later. The product is right; the test assumes the release is immediate.",
    "2. engine/tests/test_model_jobs.py::test_verify_drops_a_changed_file_so_the_next_download_fetches_only_it failed once under the full suite (download refused busy right after verify's model.done) and passed 10 of 10 alone. In oneframe/models/jobs.py, _work emits the ending event before _run's finally releases the store lock and clears _job, so a client that starts the next job on model.done can be refused busy.",
    "3. Ctrl+C under npm run: in 2 of 5 stops (MoGe-2, MoGe-3's vitg) PowerShell's prompt came back before the tool printed its last lines ('stopped', 'model.stopped'), which then appeared after the prompt. The journals ended in model.stopped and no process was left, but npm itself does not wait for the tool as scripts/tool.js does; a download typed again at once could be refused locked."
  ],
